# SPECTRE

Self-coordinating Penetration and Exploit Crew for Threat Research and Exposure. Multi-agent lab pen testing with a visual demo UI.

## Stack

- **Orchestration:** Python 3.12+ (`spectre/`) — asyncio, Pydantic schemas, LangGraph or custom event loop (decide at Phase 1)
- **Demo UI:** Vite + React 18+ + TypeScript (strict) in `src/`
- **Lab targets:** Docker Compose in `targets/`
- **Streaming:** WebSocket from orchestrator to UI
- Do not introduce cloud infra, C2, or real-world target lists unless explicitly requested

## Safety (non-negotiable)

- **Authorized lab targets only** — every engagement requires `scope.yaml` with explicit allowlist
- Tools and orchestrator **must reject** out-of-scope hosts before execution
- Never scan, exploit, or document real-world systems without explicit written authorization in scope config
- Audit log every tool invocation, finding, and handoff

## Code style

- Python: type hints, Pydantic models for bus schemas, `async` tool wrappers
- TypeScript: functional React components, named exports for utilities
- Smallest correct diff; no unrelated refactors
- Agent prompts and tool configs live in `spectre/agents/` — not scattered magic strings

## Architecture rules

- **Bus-first coordination** — agents publish to Findings Bus; no direct agent-to-agent calls
- **Orchestrator owns handoffs** — activation logic in `spectre/orchestrator/`, logged with human-readable reasons
- **Sandboxed tools** — all offensive tooling wrapped in `spectre/tools/` with scope checks and timeouts
- **Separation** — Python orchestration in `spectre/`; demo UI in `src/`; lab targets in `targets/`

## File naming

- `PascalCase` — React components (`AgentChatPanel.tsx`)
- `camelCase` — TS hooks/utilities (`useFindingsStream.ts`)
- `snake_case` — Python modules (`findings_bus.py`)
- `kebab-case` — docs and config (`local-arch-overview.md`, `scope.yaml`)

## Async I/O (required)

- Python: `asyncio`, async subprocess for tools, async WebSocket server
- Frontend: async fetch/WebSocket; never block UI thread with sync parsing of large payloads
- Heavy report generation: async or background task with progress events

## Testing (required per feature)

- Minimum **1 positive** and **3 negative** tests per new feature
- Python: `pytest` in `tests/` or colocated `test_*.py`
- Frontend: `vitest` colocated `*.test.ts`
- Include out-of-scope rejection tests for any tool wrapper or agent action

## Stop on breakage (required)

If tests, types, lint, or build fail: **stop** current work, **fix** immediately, verify green, then resume

## Documentation (required)

- Document every feature in `docs/local/local-<area>-<topic>.md`
- Index new docs in `docs/local/README.md`
- Use `.cursor/skills/document-feature/` template

## Git workflow (required)

- **Issue first** — open a GitHub issue before starting work
- **Branch** — `feature|fix|chore/<issue>-<slug>` from latest `main`
- **PR only** — never commit directly to `main`; open PR with summary, test plan, `Closes #<issue>`
- Small focused commits; imperative messages; no secrets or generated artifacts
- See `.cursor/skills/git-workflow/` and `docs/local/local-dev-git-workflow.md`

## Scope guard

- v1 is DVWA lab demo with four-agent crew and handoff visualization
- No HackTheBox automation, cloud deployment, or credential harvesting beyond lab scope unless explicitly requested
- See [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) and `.cursor/skills/` for architecture and workflows
